# Training-universe file — universe-breadth prep (--symbols-file)
#
# Format: one symbol per line. '#' starts a comment (full-line or trailing);
# blank lines are ignored; duplicates are dropped keeping first occurrence;
# case is preserved (crypto pairs like BTC/USD are allowed but note that
# `backfill bars` routes them to `backfill crypto-bars`).
#
# Purpose: widen the TRAINING panel far beyond the 55-name trading universe.
# Cross-sectional models learn from breadth — 500+ names give the ranker a
# real cross-section per date instead of 54. Training on a wider universe
# than you trade is STANDARD quant practice: the model learns general
# structure from breadth; the portfolio still only ever holds the vetted
# trading universe (which stays 55 and is NOT changed by this file).
#
# Usage (once Tiingo Power is active — the free tier will throttle/refuse
# a 500-name daily-history backfill):
#   python -m dynamo.cli.backfill bars --start 2020-01-01 --end 2026-08-01 \
#       --symbols-file config/training_universe.txt
#   python -m dynamo.cli.backfill fundamentals --symbols-file ... (n/a yet —
#       fundamentals takes --symbols/--universe; use the seed-ciks path)
#   python -m dynamo.cli.quant_train --train-start 2024-01-01 \
#       --train-end 2026-06-30 --label breadth-v1 \
#       --symbols-file config/training_universe.txt
#
# SURVIVORSHIP BIAS — read before building this file:
#   Using TODAY'S constituent list for a historical training window is
#   survivorship-biased: names that were delisted, acquired, or dropped from
#   the index during the window are missing, and today's members are, by
#   construction, the winners. Effects on THIS pipeline:
#     * the ranker's label distribution skews positive (losers vanished);
#     * the downside classifier under-sees blowups (the exact events it
#       should learn);
#   Mitigations (documented, in order of strength):
#     1. Prefer a point-in-time constituent list for the training-window
#        start (e.g. an archived index membership snapshot) and INCLUDE the
#        since-delisted names — Tiingo serves delisted tickers' history.
#     2. If only today's list is available, keep the walk-forward report
#        card's honesty checks in mind: the survivorship lift inflates
#        absolute IC but affects model AND baselines alike; the ship gates
#        compare against baselines on the SAME panel, which cancels much
#        (not all) of the bias.
#     3. Record the list provenance and snapshot date in the tuning log for
#        every trained label (docs/tuning_log_campaign_v3.md convention).
#   The trading universe is unaffected either way — it stays the vetted 55.
#
# Example large-cap list (S&P 100-style; REPLACE with your provenance-tracked
# list and note its snapshot date in the tuning log):
